# `concepts/` — AI style reference only

`concepts/` exists so the AI can **look** at frames + `ART_DIRECTION.md` and **match** the notebook-pencil look. It is **not** part of the game or of development.

## Must

- Before changing menu/battle/UI look, **read** `concepts/ART_DIRECTION.md` and the relevant concept frames
- Ship playable art only under `assets/` or colocated in `src/` (features / scenes / `src/ui/`)
- Keep Godot blind to the folder: `concepts/.gdignore` + every export preset `exclude_filter` includes `concepts/*`

## Never

- `res://concepts/...` in `.tscn`, `.tres`, `.gd`, preload, `@export`, or `ResourceLoader`
- Copy, move, or generate **into the running game** from `concepts/` (no pipeline, no `tools/` reading it as a source of shipped files)
- Put game scenes, scripts, `.tres`, or runtime audio in `concepts/`
- Assign concept files in the Godot inspector
- Treat `concepts/` as a texture pack, HUD kit, or shared `assets/` stand-in

If a visual is needed in play: recreate or place a **separate** file under `assets/` or the feature/scene `ui/` folder. Leave `concepts/` untouched except as a look reference.
